T WrittenPixel            | VisibilitySurface.slang | 25-29   | contract                  | -  | What one fragment writes — the two colour targets this recording produces at the resolved pixel. and a fragment writing it explicitly surrenders the early comparison the whole arrangement rests on — every fragment shaded before its depth is known, on a document whose entire purpose is to resolve the visible surface before anything shades at all. between this projection and the previous rotation's and no previous projection has crossed the device edge yet. `16` §4.2 places it in this recording and `64` §8 depends on it; it lands with the second transform, and the recording declares three attachments until it does.
    has   SV_Target0  Unsigned32x2 Written :  [-]  ?
    has   SV_Target1  Real32 Occupancy :      [-]  ?
    note  🔴 Depth is not among them. It is the recorded comparison's own output under `VK_COMPARE_OP_GREATER`,
    note  ⚠️ 🚧 `MotionSurface` is `08` §2's fourth production and is absent here, because it is the difference

