T ObjectPosition          | VisibilityUniform.slang | 90-95   | contract                  | -  | One vertex position in its occupant's own object space, narrowed at the upload. survive every rotation and the view origin moves every rotation, so a span carrying view-relative positions would have to be rewritten whenever the camera moved — the one cost `16` §1 exists to avoid. occupant's placement with `46`'s projection at 64 bits, with `02`'s `Rebase` applied to the placement's translation before anything narrows, and only the composed coefficients cross at 32 bits. That ordering is the whole point: subtracting the view origin after a truncation is what `02` calls jitter with a plausible-looking cause, and folding it into the translation places the subtraction before the narrowing. bounded by the occupant and a 32-bit real resolves it far below `38`'s welding tolerance; a document position carries the placement as well, and that is what exhausts the width.
    has   PositionX  Real32  [-]  ?
    has   PositionY  Real32  [-]  ?
    has   PositionZ  Real32  [-]  ?
    by    Shader/VisibilityCorner.slang
    note  🔴 Object space and **not** rebased, which is what lets the span persist. `16` §1 makes the residency
    note  🔴 The rebasing is therefore in the **transform** rather than in the position. The host composes the
    note  ⚠️ Narrowing an object-space position is safe where narrowing a document one is not. An object extent is

T DrawnTriangle           | VisibilityUniform.slang | 103-111 | contract                  | -  | One drawn triangle — which partition it belongs to and its ordinal within that partition. A partition carries 64 to 128 triangles, so the ordinal fits a narrow range and the pair fits the two components `08` §2 claims `VisibilityIndex` as. Counting document-wide would exhaust the component on a document of a few million triangles and leave nothing for the partition.
    has   CornerVertex0     Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    has   CornerVertex1     Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    has   CornerVertex2     Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    has   PartitionOrdinal  Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    has   TriangleOrdinal   Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    has   Unoccupied        Unsigned32  [-]  ?
    by    Shader/VisibilityCorner.slang
    note  🔴 The triangle ordinal counts **within the partition** and never within the document, per `16` §4.

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                    WHAT IS CARRIED
