T ResolvedCorner          | VisibilityUniform.slang | 122-127 | contract                  | -  | What the vertex entry point resolves and the fragment entry point writes. ordinal across a triangle produces a fractional ordinal at every pixel but the corners, which resolves to whichever partition the rounding reaches and reads as an image speckled with a neighbour's surface.
    has   SV_Position  Real32x4 ClipPosition :                        [-]  ?
    has   PARTITION    nointerpolation Unsigned32 PartitionOrdinal :  [-]  ?
    has   TRIANGLE     nointerpolation Unsigned32 TriangleOrdinal :   [-]  ?
    by    Shader/VisibilityCorner.slang, Shader/VisibilitySurface.slang
    note  🔴 Both ordinals are carried **flat**. They are ordinals and not quantities: interpolating a partition

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     THE PROJECTION
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

F ProjectObjectPosition   | VisibilityUniform.slang | 149-174 | nonallocating,nonthrowing | ✔️ | Projects one object-space position through the composed transform. applied with an implicit unit fourth ordinate rather than with a stored one — the position is a point and never a direction, so the alternative is a component that is unity at every call site. bits by the host and narrowed once. One product per corner and no second transform: a shader applying a placement and then a projection has narrowed the intermediate, and that intermediate is the document position whose width `02` rebases precisely to avoid spending. negating a depth after the projection has reversed it has reversed it twice, and the image is the inside of every object rather than an image that sorts wrongly.
    in    Projecting  VisibilityUniform  [-]   the uniform block, for its coefficients
    in    Positioned  ObjectPosition     [mm]  the position, in the occupant's own object space
    out   -           Clipped            [-]   the clip position, the perspective divide not yet applied
    by    Shader/VisibilityCorner.slang
    note  📐 Column-major, matching `02`'s `ProjectedTransform`. The fourth column is the translation and it is
    note  🔴 The transform carries the occupant's placement, the rebasing and `46`'s projection, composed at 64
    note  🔴 The reversed depth convention is `46`'s and lives in the projection itself, not here. A shader
